    <!-- ═══ OVERVIEW ═══ -->
    <div id="panel-overview" class="tab-panel active">
      <div class="sec">
        <div class="plain-summary">
          <button class="share-btn" onclick="foraShare(this)" title="Share" aria-label="Share"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="18" cy="5" r="3"/><circle cx="6" cy="12" r="3"/><circle cx="18" cy="19" r="3"/><line x1="8.59" y1="13.51" x2="15.42" y2="17.49"/><line x1="15.41" y1="6.51" x2="8.59" y2="10.49"/></svg></button>
          <strong>GAESA in plain language:</strong> GAESA is the Cuban military's business empire. Created by Raúl Castro in the 1990s to give the armed forces a revenue base after the Soviet Union collapsed. It now controls Cuba's hotels, largest bank, biggest port, supermarkets, gas stations, and remittance businesses — roughly 37% of the entire Cuban economy. The Cuban government does not audit GAESA. Its profits go to Cuba's military and ruling elite, not into the national budget. The US sanctioned GAESA on May 7, 2026, calling it a conglomerate that "steals millions in aid for the Cuban people at the behest of the regime." The Cuban government rarely acknowledges GAESA exists.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sec">
        <div class="sec-ey">Structural Paradox</div>
        <h2 class="sec-headline">A Marxist State Running a Corporate Empire — in Secret</h2>
        <p class="sec-lead">GAESA operates inside a country whose government publicly condemns capitalism, private property, and corporate profit — while itself functioning as an opaque, capitalist-style conglomerate, with subsidiaries incorporated in Panama, Cyprus, and Liberia specifically to move money outside the socialist system it supposedly supports.</p>
        <div class="money-flow">
          <div class="mf-label">How money is supposed to flow vs. how it actually flows</div>
          <div class="mf-flow">
            <div class="mf-node"><div class="mf-icon">🏨</div><div class="mf-name">Tourism revenue</div></div>
            <div class="mf-arrow">→</div>
