        <h2 class="sec-headline">The Numbers — Disputed, But Documented</h2>
        <p class="sec-lead">GAESA does not publish accounts. What is known comes from two sources: a 2025 leak of internal 2023–2024 financial statements published by El Nuevo Herald, and the US State Department's May 2026 sanctions announcement. The figures differ. At least one economist disputes both as inflated. The Cuban government says nothing.</p>
        <div class="assets-panel">
          <div class="ap-title">Three Reported Figures — All Disputed by Cuba</div>
          <div class="ap-text">All three figures come from outside GAESA. Cuba has never acknowledged GAESA's financial structure publicly. The dispute between the Herald's figure and the UCL economist's assessment is itself part of the documented record — FORA presents the disagreement, not a resolution.</div>
